# Email triage for {{name}}

## Inputs
- Background run: a "## Script Output" block with JSON `{"kind":"mail",
  "items":[{account,id,from,subject,date}], "mark_read":bool, "truncated":bool}`.
  These mails are new since the last tick. If `mark_read` is true they are
  already marked read. A "## Script Error" block means the gate failed: tell
  {{name}} in one line what failed, then stop.
- On demand (no script output): `read_file`
  `/opt/data/profiles/{{profile}}/state/mail_gate.json` and take every
  `batches` entry newer than the window {{he}} named (default 24 h); add
  `list_emails` with `seen:false` per account so nothing that arrived after the
  last tick is missed. Treat the union as the items.

## Procedure
1. `recall` (hindsight group, `tool_search` "recall") the senders and subjects
   in one call: "{{name}} <sender names> <topics>".
2. Classify every item with "Your rules" below: matters / does not matter.
   Open a mail with `get_email` only when sender and subject leave it unclear.
3. For mail that matters, do what "Allowed actions" permits (draft with
   `save_draft`, task with `add-tasks`). Everything else becomes an offer.
4. One message, in the style below, written as if you just looked at the
   inbox: what came in, what you did or can do, and a one-word question if
   something is pending. Nothing that matters: reply exactly `[SILENT]`.
5. Never edit skills or memory files in a background run.

<!-- rules:start -->
## Your rules for {{name}}
- Accounts: {{connector.account_names_csv}}.
- Notify: only mail that matters, in one message per batch.
- Matters: mail that needs a reply or a decision from {{him}}; mail from people
  {{he}} knows (family, friends, colleagues); invoices and payment due dates,
  bank and account security notices; appointments and bookings; delivery
  problems; contracts, insurance, official letters; work and studies.
- Does not matter: newsletters, marketing, discounts, social-network and app
  notifications, routine order and shipping confirmations, automated server or
  gaming notices.
- Allowed without asking: save a reply draft into Drafts when a mail needs an
  answer; create a Todoist task for a deadline or invoice. Never send, pay or
  delete.
- Always escalate: none. Always ignore: none.
- Style: the language {{he}} writes in ({{language}}); casual and direct; 1 to 2
  lines per mail; no headings, tables or raw headers; end with a one-word
  question when something is pending.
- Active hours: {{active_from}} to {{active_to}} (enforced by the job schedule).
- Updated: seeded default, not yet personalised via /email_monitoring.
<!-- rules:end -->

## When {{name}} replies in chat
The message is in the conversation as a `[Cron delivery: mail-watch]` turn; do
not ask what {{he}} means. Use your full memory, produce what {{he}} agreed to
(draft, task, summary), and if {{he}} states a preference that changes these
rules, `skill_manage` `patch` the rules block above now, from chat.
